@startuml
' ISJ107V Assignment 3 - document lifecycle state machine
skinparam backgroundColor #FFFFFF
skinparam shadowing false
skinparam defaultFontName Carlito
skinparam defaultFontSize 12
skinparam state {
  BorderColor #1F3864
  BackgroundColor #F4F7FB
  FontColor #17233D
}
skinparam ArrowColor #1F3864

title Figure 7: State Machine Diagram - LegalDocument Processing Lifecycle

[*] --> PENDING : upload accepted\n(consent recorded, file encrypted)

PENDING : Document row created
PENDING : Ciphertext written to store
PENDING : Awaiting a free worker

PENDING --> PROCESSING : worker dequeues job

PROCESSING : Text extracted per page\n(PDFBox / Apache POI)
PROCESSING : NLP field extraction
PROCESSING : Validation against target case

PROCESSING --> FAILED : no machine-readable text\n[scanned image only]
PROCESSING --> REJECTED : validation fails\n[wrong matter or no case content]
PROCESSING --> PROCESSED : validation passes\nand summary generated

FAILED : rejectionReason =\n"No extractable text"
FAILED : Retry action offered to lawyer

REJECTED : rejectionReason recorded
REJECTED : Conflicting spans highlighted
REJECTED : Listed in admin rejection report
REJECTED : Extractions retained for review

PROCESSED : Extractions persisted\n(confidence · span · page)
PROCESSED : Draft summary created
PROCESSED : Deadlines derived from dates

FAILED --> PROCESSING : retry AI\n(POST /api/documents/{id}/retry)\n[stale results discarded]
REJECTED --> PROCESSING : re-file against correct case\nand retry

PROCESSED --> [*] : summary approved\nand released to client
REJECTED --> [*] : document deleted by lawyer
FAILED --> [*] : document deleted by lawyer

note right of PROCESSED
  Only a PROCESSED document whose summary
  has been explicitly approved by a legal
  practitioner becomes visible in the client
  portal (FR-06).
end note

note left of REJECTED
  REJECTED is a terminal-but-recoverable state:
  the document is blocked from the client view
  yet its extractions remain visible to the
  lawyer so the mis-filing can be diagnosed.
end note

@enduml
